  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The tool's current evaluation relies on simulated or proxy inputs rather than real-world transport, vessel, and ecological data.",
      "what": "The study develops a modular cost-benefit analysis tool that calculates Net-Present-Values and Benefit-Cost-Ratios for individual and combined waterway bottlenecks, using a Greedy-Algorithm to rank and prioritize rehabilitation projects along a transport corridor.",
      "why": "It demonstrates a strong path dependency in waterway infrastructure investments, proving that isolated bottleneck removals are mostly ineffective and that economic benefits are only unlocked when all interconnected bottlenecks along a corridor are rehabilitated."
    }
